2. UTC vs asOf-Location -- WORKER'S CLAIM VERIFIED (PASS)
=====================================================================
Independent variant "varlocal": asOfDay = dayOf(asOf) and
occ = dayOf(rp.NextExpected.In(asOf.Location())) -- i.e. normalise both sides
into asOf's Location, the alternative the worker rejected.
  cd <scratch>/varlocal && TZ=America/New_York go test -count=1 -run TestZZProbeLeadRepro -v ./internal/services/accounts/
  PROBE yearly  crossing=(none)     minimum=800.00 topup=0.00
  PROBE monthly crossing=2026-10-01 minimum=700.00 topup=100.00
Identical to the broken attempt-1 output. Converting the occurrence into
Asia/Tokyo puts 2026-09-01 00:00 UTC at 2026-09-01 09:00 JST, whose day label is
asOf's OWN day (2026-09-01 JST) -- the day the walk deliberately skips -- so the
occurrence is advanced past by `!occ.After(asOfDay)` and never scheduled. The
two normalisations are NOT equivalent and the worker's stated reason
(projection.go:178-182) is factually right for this fixture.

